    {
      "id": "claim_427424d60a104b31a8c50588355a72c5",
      "statement": "internal/middleware/logging.go's NewLogger is a general-purpose, global chi HTTP access-log middleware (registered via router.Use before the /api/v0/trusted-actions route group) that logs one \"Request completed\" line per request for every route including /health; because its log message is not \"audit record\", it is excluded from the CloudWatch subscription filter that feeds the Firehose/S3 audit pipeline even though it writes to the same /ecs/${var.app_name} log group, making it distinct from both the AuditEntry middleware and the audit.Record executor trail.",
